    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Yamaha Previews the Future of the Tenere Adventure Bikes With Mysterious 4 Concept\nThis Rendered GT Looks a Lot Better Than Anything Jaguar Currently Makes\n16 photos\nPhoto: Instagram | alex_12_avo\nDo you remember when Jaguar used to make nice cars? You likely do, as it hasn’t been that long since that happened.\nHowever, this otherwise iconic British brand is now trying to reinvent itself and position further upmarket in an attempt to take a swing at Bentley and Rolls-Royce. And it has the Type 01 for that, an unconventional electric vehicle that does not care about anything the automaker once stood for.\nPreviewed by the Type 00 Concept, it was unveiled earlier this year, and does not look like any other road-legal Jaguar out there. There’s no traditional grille at the front, it features high shoulder lines, and if it weren’t for the panoramic roof, then the cockpit would have felt more like a tomb. There’s no rear window, and the cabin looks like it came from the space age.\nThe order books for the Jaguar 01 are expected to open in 2027, with the model expected to start at $130,000 in our market, and 130,000 pounds (equal to $171,190) in the UK. It features three electric motors for a total of 1,015 hp and 1,007 lb-ft (1,365 Nm) of torque, and it has an EPA range of 400 miles (644 km), according to Jag’, with its 118 kWh NMC battery pack fully charged.\nPhoto: Instagram | alex_12_avo Jaguar has clearly been criticized for attempting to reinvent itself, especially since the 01 does not look like anything it has even come from this company’s portfolio, and only time will tell if this was the right move. In the meantime, the rendering world, or a small chunk of it to be more precise, keeps imagining various Jaguar projects that will never see the light of day.\nOne of the latest to have crossed our screens can be seen in the gallery above. It has @alex_12_avo behind it, and was shared on social media earlier this week. The pixel-infused model is simply called the Jaguar GT , and to be honest, it definitely looks like an everyday grand tourer that one would expect to encounter at the golf course.\nIt features a very exotic overall design, with a vented hood, a pair of LED headlights, a large grille flanked by a pair of vents, an aggressive profile, muscular wheel arches, broad shoulders, and a back-end that looks more like an Aston Martin than a Jag’, this writer believes.\nNevertheless, that doesn’t make it any less exciting, and to be honest, this thing does indeed look a lot better than anything Jaguar currently makes, as mentioned in the title. And by that, we clearly mean the 01. So, if you had to choose between the quirky Jaguar 01 with its EV powertrain and this rendered GT that features ICE power, what color would the latter have? View this post on Instagram A post shared by Alexander (@alex_12_avo)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\njaguar grand tourer Jaguar Type 01 Type 01 electric vehicles rendering renderings\nAbout the author: Cristian Gnaticov\nAfter a series of unfortunate events put an end to Cristian's dream of entering a custom built & tuned old-school Dacia into a rally competition, he moved on to drive press cars and write for a living. He's worked for several automotive online journals and now he's back at autoevolution after his first tour in the mid-2000s. Full profile\nUP NEXT 1963 Buick Found in a Barn in Nebraska Begs for Restoration—and It's Unexpectedly Complete",
